DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=82949\nhttps://sites.dartmouth.edu/health-econlab/symposium/join-
 us-at-the-health-policy-and-economics-symposium/\nhttps://sites.dartmouth.
 edu/health-econlab/symposium/\nhttps://experience.arcgis.com/experience/0a
 845c134d0946649607620ab0b1afe5/\nhttps://www.dartmouth.edu/transportation/
 parking/cost_information/visitors.php\n\nDescription:\nPlease join us for 
 the\nHealth Policy and Economics Symposium on October 8\, 12:00 to 5:00 pm
 .\nCook Auditorium\, A02 Murdough Center. Access the auditorium via the I
 rving Institute\nFree and open to all. Lunch and refreshments will be serv
 ed.\nPlease use this\nlink to RSVP.\nResearchers\, clinicians\, and organi
 zation leaders will discuss pressing issues in health\, health policy\, an
 d health economics.\nThe symposium will feature five panels: 1) maternal h
 ealth\, disparities\, and outcomes\, 2) US prescription drug pricing\, 3) 
 social determinants of health and health safety nets\, 4) substance use an
 d mental health care in New England\, and 5) primary care access and short
 ages.\nPlease share this event with your colleagues.\nThe event is designe
 d for a broad audience\, with a focus on welcoming regional stakeholders\,
  researchers\, health professionals\, students\, faculty\, and others inte
 rested in these topics.\nFor more information\, please\nsee our website\n.
  Please use this\nlink to RSVP.\nLocation and Parking\nCook Auditorium is 
 located in room A02 at the Murdough Center at 100 Tuck Mall\, Hanover\, NH
 . Please access the auditorium via the Irving Institute.\nSee the Dartmout
 h Campus Map for more information.\nPublic Parking on Campus\nThe Emily an
 d Errik Anderson Parking Garage is located at 15 Thayer Drive\, Hanover\, 
 NH.\nSee the Dartmouth Transportation Services page for more campus parkin
 g information.\n\nSponsor / organizer: Dartmouth Institute for Health Poli
 cy & Clinical Practice\n\nAudience: Public\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nWhy thi
 s was included: explicit food-service wording\; food keyword near service 
 context\n\nFood availability is inferred from the source listing\; verify 
 details before attending.
