 th.edu/register/?id=2a6c8ea4-38f9-4b9b-9d25-4b1f72d0ae91\nhttps://guarinig
 rad.dartmouth.edu\n\nDescription:\nWalk Around Occom Pond\nJoin the Assist
 ant Dean of Guarini Graduate Student Affairs for a reflective walk around 
 Occom Pond\, followed by a coffee or tea break at Ramekin. This event offe
 rs a chance to connect with fellow graduate students\, postdocs and facult
 y in a relaxed\, natural setting\, promoting well-being and community spir
 it. You can receive a $6 coupon for Ramekin (limited to one each).\nMeet i
 n front of the Guarini School\, Anonymous Hall – across from Ramekin Caf
 e.\nGuariniGRAD Dialogues\nare a series of events designed to bring gradua
 te students\, postdocs\, and faculty together in informal settings to fost
 er empathy\, understanding\, and a deeper sense of community. By creating 
 spaces where differing views\, perspectives\, and circumstances can be sha
 red and appreciated\, these dialogues aim to strengthen connections within
  the Dartmouth community and foster a sense of belonging.\n*Guarini gradua
 te students include all PhD\, MA\, MALS\, MET\, and MFA students\; and MS 
 students in Engineering\, Computer Science\, and Earth Sciences.\n\nSponso
 r / organizer: GuariniGRAD\n\nAudience: Guarini graduate students and post
 docs\n\nSource: Guarini\n\nWhy this was included: food keyword near servic
 e context in summary\n\nFood availability is inferred from the source list
 ing\; verify details before attending.
