 ttps://irving.dartmouth.edu/research/faculty-seminar-series\n\nDescription
 :\nJoin the Dartmouth Climate Collaborative\, in partnership with the Irvi
 ng Institute for Energy and Society\, for a special faculty seminar.\nSpea
 ker:\nKate Maher\n\, Professor of Earth System Science at Stanford Univers
 ity and Senior Fellow at the Woods Institute for the Environment. Professo
 r Maher's research examines the carbon cycle through multiple lenses\, fro
 m the history of atmospheric carbon dioxide and its impact on the evolutio
 n of life to strategies for sequestering carbon today.\nTalk title:\nCarbo
 n numbers without receipts: Measurement\, markets\, and climate governance
 \nSpecial guest:\nDr. Ansley Booker\, Executive Director of Dartmouth NEXT
 \, will join to share more about the university-wide initiative that is ex
 panding opportunities for students in science\, technology\, engineering\,
  and mathematics.\nRegistration is required\, and seating is limited.\nReg
 ister to attend in person or online\n.\nLunch will be served at 11:45 am. 
 The talk begins at 12 pm\, with time for Q&A at the end.\nMurdough 309 is 
 accessible via the second floor of the Irving Institute.\nSee a campus map
 \n.\nThe faculty seminar is open to the Dartmouth community of faculty\, s
 taff\, postdocs\, and graduate students.\nThank you to Dartmouth NEXT for 
 their co-sponsorship of the Faculty Seminar Series!\nLearn more about the 
 Faculty Seminar Series\n\nSponsor / organizer: Arthur L. Irving Institute 
 for Energy and Society\, Climate Collaborative\n\nAudience: Faculty\, Post
 doc\, Staff\, Students-Graduate\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nWhy this was inclu
 ded: explicit food-service wording\; food keyword near service context\n\n
 Food availability is inferred from the source listing\; verify details bef
