DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=82819\n\nDescription:\nJoin the Native American Program’s Carle
 y Malloy and Outdoor Programs’ Willow Nilsen for a guided walk and discu
 ssion through Pine Park. Learn more about the non-human communities around
  us\, and how plants and trees have provided food sources and remedies thr
 oughout their existence. We will discuss how globalization has impacted co
 mmunities throughout the Northeast\, and within the Upper Valley. We will 
 conclude the walk with a discussion and tea and treats made with ingredien
 ts abundant in fall in NH.\nWe will walk even if it is lightly raining. If
  there is a downpour\, we will let folks know when we will reschedule. Ple
 ase dress for the weather. You may want to bring a small bag or backpack w
 ith the following: hat for sun\, raincoat\, waterbottle.\nLearn more and s
 ign up: doc.dartmouth.edu/trip/10681\n\nSponsor / organizer: Native Ameri
 can Program\n\nAudience: Public\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nWhy this was inclu
 ded: food keyword near service context\n\nFood availability is inferred fr
 om the source listing\; verify details before attending.
