BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Talk by VINE Sanctuary about rehabilitating rescued animals
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261011T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261011T130000
DTSTAMP:20261008T170805Z
UID:dartmouth-groups-1633021@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://dartmouthgroups.dartmouth.edu
 /rsvp_boot?id=1633021\n\nDescription:\nJoin us for a talk by VINE Sanctuar
 y\, an LGBTQ-led farmed animal refuge that cares for more than 500 animals
  in Springfield\, Vermont. VINE stands for "Veganism Is the Next Evolution
 \," and as an ecofeminist organization\, it works for social and environme
 ntal justice alongside animal liberation.\nSince its founding in 2000\, VI
 NE has given a home to animals like ducks\, sheep\, cows\, pigeons\, chick
 ens\, emus\, and goats\, many of whom arrive carrying the effects of traum
 a. The sanctuary is best known for its work with roosters: its cofounder s
 ays VINE was the first sanctuary in the country to figure out how to rehab
 ilitate fighting roosters\, in 2002. Its method lets former fighters obser
 ve other birds from the safety of spacious cages\, acclimating to flock li
 fe and learning the social signals roosters naturally use to resolve confl
 ict. That work has provided evidence that roosters can be successfully reh
 abilitated and even adopted into new flocks.\nCome learn how VINE helps re
 scued animals heal\, what recovery looks like day to day\, and how these s
 tories challenge common assumptions about the animals we raise for food an
 d entertainment. Open to all.\nFood Provided (Lou's muffins! )\n\nSponsor 
 / organizer: Allied Scholars for Animal Protection\n\nSource: Dartmouth Gr
 oups\n\nWhy this was included: explicit food-service wording\; food keywor
 d near service context\n\nFood availability is inferred from the source li
 sting\; verify details before attending.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261008T170805Z
LOCATION:Private Location (sign in to display)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dartmouthgroups.dartmouth.edu/rsvp_boot?id=1633021
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
END:VEVENT
