BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Aurelian Craiutu\, Moderation as Political Strategy--Past and Pres
 ent
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261015T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261015T180000
DTSTAMP:20261008T170805Z
UID:dartmouth-82254@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=82254\n\nDescription:\nModeration is a contested concept that\, w
 ith surprisingly few exceptions\, is absent from our public debates. Today
 \, the single famous line that people sometimes may remember belongs to Ba
 rry Goldwater: “Extremism in the pursuit of liberty is no vice\, moderat
 ion in the pursuit of justice is no virtue.” His witty words continue to
  provoke and invite us to rethink the nature of moderation and examine its
  eclecticism. The latter can be explored by looking at the many faces of m
 oderation and the various agendas and principles moderates of all types ad
 vanced over time.\nThe lecture will address the following questions: What 
 kind of virtue is political moderation and how can we study it? What does 
 it mean to be a moderate voice in politics? What are the limits and benefi
 ts of moderation? Finally\, can moderation be a winning card in our hyper-
 polarized political world?\nCraiutu is the Arthur F. Bentley Professor and
  Chair of the Department of Political Science at Indiana University\, Bloo
 mington. His most recent book is\nWhy Not Moderation? Letters to a Young R
 adical\n(Cambridge University Press\, 2024). His talk is sponsored by the 
 Political Economy Project and the Rockefeller Center.\n\nSponsor / organiz
 er: Political Economy Project\, Rockefeller Center\n\nAudience: Public\n\n
 Source: Dartmouth\n\nWhy this was included: Free Food category\n\nFood ava
 ilability is inferred from the source listing\; verify details before atte
 nding.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261008T170805Z
LOCATION:Room 002\, Rockefeller Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://home.dartmouth.edu/events/event?event=82254
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
END:VEVENT
