BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Owen Zidar ('08\, Princeton)\, The Everywhere Millionaire
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T180000
DTSTAMP:20261008T170805Z
UID:dartmouth-82256@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=82256\n\nDescription:\nA professor of economics and public policy
  at Princeton University\, Zidar (Class of '08) will discuss his just-publ
 ished\, ground-breaking book.\nDrawing on unprecedented data from a decade
  of research and vivid real-life stories of entrepreneurs―from a self-ma
 de hot-dog stand billionaire to the heirs of an auto dealer―Zidar and co
 -author Erich Zwick reveal a surprising truth: prosperity is more attainab
 le\, more widely distributed\, and closer to home than we imagine. A multi
 tude of Americans have built staggering fortunes by running often unglamor
 ous businesses far from the spotlight. A quiet revolution in the business 
 world―the rise of “pass-through” firms like S-corporations and partn
 erships―supercharged this wealth\, channeling vast income directly to bu
 siness owners rather than traditional corporations. Sponsor\ned by the Pol
 itical Economy Project and co-sponsored by the Rockefeller Center.\n\nSpon
 sor / organizer: Political Economy Project\, Rockefeller Center\n\nAudienc
 e: Public\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nWhy this was included: Free Food categor
 y\n\nFood availability is inferred from the source listing\; verify detail
 s before attending.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261008T170805Z
LOCATION:Room 003\, Rockefeller Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://home.dartmouth.edu/events/event?event=82256
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
END:VEVENT
