BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:QHC 2026 - Queer & Sacred: An LGBTQIA+ Interfaith Dinner
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261020T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261020T193000
DTSTAMP:20261008T170805Z
UID:dartmouth-groups-1632396@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://dartmouthgroups.dartmouth.edu
 /rsvp_boot?id=1632396\n\nDescription:\nQueerness and religion are often fr
 amed as being in conflict-but lived experiences are far more complex. For 
 many LGBTQIA+ people\, faith and spirituality can be sources of identity\,
  culture\, belonging\, and liberation. For others\, religion may bring exp
 eriences of exclusion\, questioning\, or redefining their relationship wit
 h faith. What does it mean to hold identities others may see as incompatib
 le? Where do we find belonging? And how can our communities make space for
  complexity? Join us for food and conversation with the Tucker Center expl
 oring the intersections of queerness\, religion\, spirituality\, and belon
 ging. All are welcome.\nDinner Provided by Jewel of India!\nFood Provided 
 (Jewel of India)\n\nSponsor / organizer: Office of Pluralism and Leadershi
 p / The William Jewett Tucker Center for Spiritual and Ethical Life\, Tria
 ngle House\n\nSource: Dartmouth Groups\n\nWhy this was included: Free Food
  category\; explicit food-service wording\; food or meal keyword in title\
 n\nFood availability is inferred from the source listing\; verify details 
 before attending.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261008T170805Z
LOCATION:Private Location (sign in to display)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dartmouthgroups.dartmouth.edu/rsvp_boot?id=1632396
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
